: one outcome reconciliation (requestState), server answer in decisions, authoritative physical verification\n\nUnified outcome reconciliation for independent verification 39252 (R13 f6a8cbe /\na8a9767; NO-GO: F1-F3), keeping the queue architecture, identity protections and\ndurable decisions:\n\n- requestState: the ONE reconciliation of a logical request (account + request\n  id), used by the transmission gate (enqueue, claim) and by recovery after an\n  unconfirmed commit -- durable decision first, then live copies. Removal\n  invariant: an active copy is only deleted together with its decision, so\n  absence alone never means \"not saved\" (F1).\n- Decisions record the server's answer (settled accepted / rejected). One mapping\n  to submission outcomes: already-recorded (success), rejected, not-stored with\n  reason 'discarded' (never a success), outcome-unknown for unresolved evidence.\n  Home treats already-recorded as success (refresh, no retry) and shows an\n  accurate discarded message; uncertain outcomes keep the original request id.\n- Physical verification: one classification for committed and reconciled\n  discards; the FINAL verification is authoritative and earlier cleanup errors\n  are diagnostic only (F3); storage that names no request id (an unparseable v2\n  array, id-less entries/records) makes absence unverifiable ->\n  discardedUnverified, never removed (F2). No destructive cleanup.\n\nReviewer disposition, probe and logs preserved (docs/android/evidence/\nrel04-r13-independent-39252); test/rel04R14OutcomeReconciliation reproduces F1-F3\non vendored a8a9767 (negative controls), drives the real Home \"Start now\" path\n(R13 negative control: \"Couldn't log. Try again.\" + fresh-id duplicate), and the\noutcome and cleanup matrices. Chromium CH16 covers the real cross-tab case.\nR11 X1 and one replay-reconciliation source check updated to the F2 rule and the\nclaim-bound settle line. No format, migration, origin, worker or auth change;\nrel04R4SsrA